[24.945263, "o", "run-a -> run-b\r\n\u001b[33m~ changed  [finding]\u001b[0m  Verified: go test ./... passes, 214/214.\r\n  was:      Verified: go test ./... passes locally, 214/214.\r\n\u001b[32m+ added    [fix]   \u001b[0m  In summary, the flaky parser test is fixed for good:\r\n\u001b[32m+ added    [finding]\u001b[0m  Root cause: CountTokens in internal/parser/parser.go double-counted the trailing newline via the i == len(s) sentinel iteration.\r\n\u001b[32m+ added    [fix]   \u001b[0m  Fix: corrected the loop boundary at parser.go:41 and added a regression case to parser_test.go.\r\n\u001b[31m- removed  [finding]\u001b[0m  Summary of the first investigation:\r\n\u001b[31m- removed  [finding]\u001b[0m  Root cause: the test shares mutable parser state with TestCountTokensBasic and only flakes when the two run back to back.\r\n\u001b[31m- removed  [fix]   \u001b[0m  Fix: added a warm-cache guard that skips the test when the shared state is dirty.\r\n  1 claims unchanged\r\n"]
